Relevant tables / columns and why they matter  
• PRODUCTS  
  - "id": used to join with ORDER_ITEMS."product_id"  
  - "category": to isolate ‘Sleep & Lounge’ items  
  - "cost": unit cost that will be summed and used for profit calculations  
  - "retail_price": can be compared with "sale_price" for sanity checks  

• ORDER_ITEMS  
  - "product_id": foreign key to PRODUCTS."id"  
  - "sale_price": revenue‑per‑unit that will be summed as total sales  
  - "status": filter for “Complete” records  
  - "created_at": time stamp (µs) to keep only rows between 2023‑01‑01 and 2023‑12‑31  
  - "order_id": lets us count unique completed orders  
  - "user_id": extra dimension if user level analysis is needed  

• ORDERS (optional cross‑check)  
  - "order_id": primary key; could be used to double‑validate status = 'Complete'  
  - "created_at": another time field if order‑level filtering is preferred  

Typical conditions that will be applied later  
1. PRODUCTS."category" ILIKE '%Sleep%Lounge%'   -- fuzzy match for target category  
2. ORDER_ITEMS."status" = 'Complete'  
3. ORDER_ITEMS."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 /* 2023‑01‑01 */  
                              AND     1704067199000000 /* 2023‑12‑31 23:59:59 */  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progressively build understanding—from very simple to nearly the final aggregation—while obeying the requested formatting rules.

```sql
--Description: 1) List all distinct product categories to verify spelling/format of “Sleep & Lounge”.
SELECT DISTINCT "category"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Quickly inspect categories that look like Sleep & Lounge using a fuzzy search.
SELECT DISTINCT "category"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"
WHERE "category" ILIKE '%sleep%lounge%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Show sample products that belong to the Sleep & Lounge category.
SELECT "id", "name", "brand", "cost", "retail_price"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"
WHERE "category" ILIKE '%sleep%lounge%'
ORDER BY RANDOM()
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Grab a handful of order‑item rows regardless of category to inspect status values.
SELECT "id", "order_id", "product_id", "status", "created_at", "sale_price"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
ORDER BY RANDOM()
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Join ORDER_ITEMS with PRODUCTS for Sleep & Lounge items only (any year).
SELECT oi."id",
       oi."order_id",
       oi."created_at",
       oi."sale_price",
       p."cost"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"      p
     ON oi."product_id" = p."id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%sleep%lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Same as above but restricted to records created in 2023 (micro‑second epoch).
SELECT oi."id",
       oi."order_id",
       oi."created_at",
       oi."sale_price",
       p."cost"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"      p
     ON oi."product_id" = p."id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%sleep%lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 AND 1704067199000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Compute profit per item for a sample of 2023 rows.
SELECT oi."id",
       oi."order_id",
       (oi."sale_price" - p."cost") AS "profit"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"      p
     ON oi."product_id" = p."id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%sleep%lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 AND 1704067199000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Show month, total sales and total cost (simple aggregation) for 2023 Sleep & Lounge.
SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1000000)) AS "month",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")                                    AS "total_sales",
       SUM(p."cost")                                           AS "total_cost"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"      p
     ON oi."product_id" = p."id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%sleep%lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 AND 1704067199000000
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Extend the previous query by also counting distinct complete orders per month.
SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1000000)) AS "month",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")                                    AS "total_sales",
       SUM(p."cost")                                           AS "total_cost",
       COUNT(DISTINCT oi."order_id")                           AS "num_complete_orders"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"      p
     ON oi."product_id" = p."id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%sleep%lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 AND 1704067199000000
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final‑style report with profit and profit‑to‑cost ratio for each 2023 month.
SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1000000))                AS "month",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")                                                     AS "total_sales",
       SUM(p."cost")                                                            AS "total_cost",
       COUNT(DISTINCT oi."order_id")                                            AS "num_complete_orders",
       SUM(oi."sale_price" - p."cost")                                          AS "total_profit",
       CASE WHEN SUM(p."cost") = 0 THEN NULL
            ELSE SUM(oi."sale_price" - p."cost") / SUM(p."cost") END            AS "profit_to_cost_ratio"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"      p
     ON oi."product_id" = p."id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%sleep%lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 AND 1704067199000000
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

